1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,422
Welcome to Plant Technology training.

2
00:00:02,672 --> 00:00:11,450
In this short module you will learn what feed raw materials are made of, and why that matters for the work we do in the mill.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,290
Every machine in our plant exists to handle, change or protect raw materials.

4
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:25,061
When you understand the material, you understand why each process step and each piece of equipment is there.

5
00:00:25,311 --> 00:00:29,450
This helps you troubleshoot, maintain and optimize the plant.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,953
Every raw material arrives as fresh matter.

7
00:00:34,203 --> 00:00:38,743
Fresh matter has two parts: water and dry matter.

8
00:00:38,993 --> 00:00:44,510
Water is the moisture in the material, both free and bound.

9
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:51,450
Its role is as a solvent for transport, and we measure it in kilograms.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,489
Dry matter holds all the nutritional value of the feed.

11
00:00:56,739 --> 00:01:05,450
It breaks down into five groups: carbohydrates, lipids, proteins, minerals, and other active substances.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:13,085
Carbohydrates and lipids are the energy sources, measured in megajoules.

13
00:01:13,335 --> 00:01:24,496
Carbohydrates include sugar for quick energy, starch for sustained energy, and crude fiber for digestive health.

14
00:01:24,746 --> 00:01:27,450
Lipids are the fats and oils.

15
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,452
Proteins and minerals are building materials, measured in grams.

16
00:01:33,702 --> 00:01:41,917
Amino acids, the building blocks of protein, are used for muscle, tissue and enzyme production.

17
00:01:42,167 --> 00:01:51,450
Minerals include major elements like calcium and phosphorus, and trace elements like iron, zinc and copper.

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,077
Finally, active substances: vitamins, hormones, enzymes and flavoring agents.

19
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:07,450
They are used in very small amounts, measured in milligrams, but they have a big effect.

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:23,910
To recap: water for transport, carbohydrates and lipids for energy, proteins and minerals for building, and active substances in milligrams.

21
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:29,450
Now take the short quiz to complete this module.

